// Title: Renamed AutoIt Execution
// ID: f4264e47-f522-4c38-a420-04525d5b880f
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-06-04
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1027
// Description: Detects the execution of a renamed AutoIt2.exe or AutoIt3.exe.
// AutoIt is a scripting language and automation tool for Windows systems. While primarily used for legitimate automation tasks, it can be misused in cyber attacks.
// Attackers can leverage AutoIt to create and distribute malware, including keyloggers, spyware, and botnets. A renamed AutoIt executable is particularly suspicious.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((src.process.cmdline containsCIS " /AutoIt3ExecuteScript" OR src.process.cmdline containsCIS " /ErrorStdOut")) OR ((Hashes containsCIS "IMPHASH=FDC554B3A8683918D731685855683DDF" OR Hashes containsCIS "IMPHASH=CD30A61B60B3D60CECDB034C8C83C290" OR Hashes containsCIS "IMPHASH=F8A00C72F2D667D2EDBB234D0C0AE000")) OR ((OriginalFileName = "AutoIt3.exe" OR OriginalFileName = "AutoIt2.exe" OR OriginalFileName = "AutoIt.exe"))) AND NOT (((src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\AutoIt.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\AutoIt2.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\AutoIt3_x64.exe" OR src.process.image.path endswithCIS "\\AutoIt3.exe"))))
